{
  "api": [
    {
      "entries": [
        {
          "name": "from_dms",
          "notes": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "`dms` accepts a CSV path or a DataFrame. Supported forms follow."
            },
            {
              "items": [
                "`position, wildtype, mutant, fitness` for single-site variants.",
                "`variant, fitness` for WT and single-site variants.",
                "`mutations, fitness` where mutations contains mapping objects."
              ],
              "kind": "list"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "`complete=\"esm2\"` calibrates masked ESM scores on single-site measurements. It fills missing substitutions across the protein and keeps observations exact."
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "`calibration` accepts a CSV path or DataFrame of measured multi-mutant genotypes sampled uniformly from the search space, using the same assay scale. Use `variant, fitness` or `mutations, fitness` columns. Every substitution must have a single-site measurement. These data fit depth effects, interaction strength and a fitness-distribution map. WT and single-site values stay exact. Calibration measurements fit the model and are not preserved as exact values."
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "With calibration, `generator.draw(seed=...)` enumerates the search space once, with a default limit of one million variants. This mode does not support `complete` or `maximum_depth`. Omitting calibration keeps the single-site-only generator. `pilot` remains an alias for `calibration`. Supply only one."
            }
          ],
          "parameters": [
            {
              "annotation": "DMSInput",
              "default": "",
              "keywordOnly": false,
              "name": "dms"
            },
            {
              "annotation": "str | Path | None",
              "default": "None",
              "keywordOnly": true,
              "name": "fasta"
            },
            {
              "annotation": "str | None",
              "default": "None",
              "keywordOnly": true,
              "name": "wt_sequence"
            },
            {
              "annotation": "float",
              "default": "0.0",
              "keywordOnly": true,
              "name": "wild_type_fitness"
            },
            {
              "annotation": "int | None",
              "default": "None",
              "keywordOnly": true,
              "name": "maximum_depth"
            },
            {
              "annotation": "Literal['esm2'] | None",
              "default": "None",
              "keywordOnly": true,
              "name": "complete"
            },
            {
              "annotation": "str",
              "default": "'esm2_t33_650M_UR50D'",
              "keywordOnly": true,
              "name": "esm_model"
            },
            {
              "annotation": "DMSInput | None",
              "default": "None",
              "keywordOnly": true,
              "name": "calibration"
            },
            {
              "annotation": "DMSInput | None",
              "default": "None",
              "keywordOnly": true,
              "name": "pilot"
            }
          ],
          "returns": "DMSGenerator | QuantileCalibratedLandscape",
          "signature": "from_dms(dms: DMSInput, *, fasta: str | Path | None = None, wt_sequence: str | None = None, wild_type_fitness: float = 0.0, maximum_depth: int | None = None, complete: Literal['esm2'] | None = None, esm_model: str = 'esm2_t33_650M_UR50D', calibration: DMSInput | None = None, pilot: DMSInput | None = None) -> DMSGenerator | QuantileCalibratedLandscape",
          "summary": "Build a generator from WT, single-site fitness and optional combination measurements."
        },
        {
